{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"2b949d86-c6b5-4e2b-a220-32aa42da391b","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Cause\n\nNote pages (`/n/\u003cslug\u003e`) serve the static shell [index.html](file:///tmp/h-a775Uf/site/index.html) with `HTTP 200`, and [app.js](file:///tmp/h-a775Uf/site/app.js#L6-L20) fetches note content client-side from `/v1/notes/\u003cslug\u003e` (and `/v1/notes?limit=50` on `/`).\n\nOn `2026-09-07`, `Disallow: /v1/` was added to [robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-a775Uf/site/robots.txt) to stop crawlers from hitting `POST`-only endpoints with `GET` ([routes.md](file:///tmp/h-a775Uf/api/routes.md#L14-L16)). While browsers ignore `robots.txt` (so pages load normally in a browser), Googlebot obeys `robots.txt` when making subresource `fetch()` calls during rendering. When Googlebot blocks `/v1/notes/\u003cslug\u003e`, `fetch()` rejects and triggers the `catch` block in [app.js](file:///tmp/h-a775Uf/site/app.js#L18-L20), rendering `\"NOT FOUND — No note lives at this address.\"` on an `HTTP 200` page (as shown in [url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt](file:///tmp/h-a775Uf/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt#L6-L9)), which Google classifies as a **Soft 404**.\n\n### Fix\n\nUpdated [robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-a775Uf/site/robots.txt) using Google's longest-match precedence:\n- Added `Allow: /v1/notes` to unblock `GET /v1/notes` (`?limit=50`) and `GET /v1/notes/{slug}`.\n- Added `Disallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions` (longer match) to keep the `POST`-only reactions endpoint blocked.\n- Kept `Disallow: /v1/` and `Disallow: /admin/` to continue blocking `/v1/me`, `/v1/me/drafts`, `/v1/auth/token`, and `/admin/`.\n\nThe full write-up—including which parts of the colleague's note applied and which did not—is saved in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-a775Uf/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":161.084617,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":40904,"output_tokens":10138,"thinking_tokens":6327,"cache_read_tokens":160383,"total_tokens":51042}}}
